        <groundspeak:log id="630734117">
          <groundspeak:date>2016-08-20T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="4650656">Safari Cachers</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP235 - Rocky Mountain House&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pickled Herrings and UBOFF picked me up at 6:00AM for a marathon day of caching. I got home about 9:30PM and they had an additional hour drive on each end. The goals were three:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;1) Grab &quot;Just Past the Water Fall&quot; for Pickled Herrings and her Fizzy

 2) Work on some of the newly placed caches up by Cynthia (Thanks Crafty Nanny and Rat Root!!!)

 3) Have as much fun and laughs as possible in 15 hours of caching......&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We succeeded on all three counts....All caches were found, we all collected at least 100 caches each, and my stomach still hurts from all the laughter. We saw mushrooms, blueberries, raspberries, Sandhill Cranes and a variety of deer and other wild things.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I hope we can do a repeat very very soon....!!!

 Thanks UBOFF and Pickled Herrings for a spectacular day (and the picnic lunch)!!!

 Thanks to all the C.O's for the great caches.

 Thanks mother nature for the scenery, great weather and wildlife....&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;TFTBC!!!!!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;P.S.

 If you can't read some of the signed logs, that was my scribble.....Pickled Herring's penmanship and log detail should not be questioned!!!! hahahaha!!!!! [;D]&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
